-- title:
--   Morphisms from a local scheme factor through one chart
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring, let $K$ be a field that is an $A$-algebra, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero. Write $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements of $K$ integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and $\mathcal O_{\infty} =$ `chartAlgInf A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$; the scheme [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229) is the pushout of the two morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusions of these two algebras into the middle chart algebra, and $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $\iota_{\infty}$ denote the associated chart morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_{\mathrm{fin}} \to \mathcal X$ and $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_{\infty} \to \mathcal X$ into this model $\mathcal X$. The assertion is: for every local ring $O$ and every morphism of schemes $g \colon \operatorname{Spec} O \to \mathcal X$, either there is a ring homomorphism $\beta \colon \mathcal O_{\mathrm{fin}} \to O$ with $g$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(\beta)$ followed by $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$, or there is a ring homomorphism $\beta \colon \mathcal O_{\infty} \to O$ with $g$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(\beta)$ followed by $\iota_{\infty}$. The homomorphisms $\beta$ are only required to be ring homomorphisms, not $A$-algebra maps.
--
--   This is the standard factorisation property of morphisms out of the spectrum of a local ring: the closed point lands in one of the two affine charts covering the model, and a morphism from a local scheme whose closed point lies in an open subscheme factors through that subscheme, hence through a ring homomorphism since the chart is affine. It is used to read off chart coordinates of local (in particular geometric) points of the two-chart model, in the analysis of cuspidal sections and of the Laurent place reduction on the $X_1$ models.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_TwoChart_exists_eq_specMap_comp_iotaFin_or_exists_eq_specMap_comp_iotaInf.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_TwoChartModel

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

theorem ModularCurve.TwoChart.exists_eq_specMap_comp_iotaFin_or_exists_eq_specMap_comp_iotaInf
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (K : Type u) [Field K] [Algebra A K] (j : K) [Fact (j ≠ 0)]
    {O : Type u} [CommRing O] [IsLocalRing O]
    (g : Spec (CommRingCat.of O) ⟶ ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j) :
    (∃ β : ↥(ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A K j) →+* O,
        g = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom β) ≫ ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin A K j) ∨
      (∃ β : ↥(ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgInf A K j) →+* O,
        g = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom β) ≫ ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιInf A K j) := by sorry
